# Decimal remainder of decimal operands

Takes 10.5 modulo 3 to verify the fractional remainder stays exact,
producing 1.5. A negative dividend verifies the remainder keeps the
dividend sign, producing -1.5.

>>> source
dividend: decimal = 10.5
divisor: decimal = 3
negative_dividend: decimal = -10.5

// Verifies the remainder of two positive decimals.
positive_remainder: decimal = dividend % divisor
print(positive_remainder)

// Verifies the remainder takes the dividend sign.
negative_remainder: decimal = negative_dividend % divisor
print(negative_remainder)

<<< stdout
1.5
-1.5

<<< stderr
